      "writtenOn": "2019-11-28T09:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not clear from the data sheet how long the read command will take.\nDoes it merely read the data registers, or does it wait the integration time to complete?\n\n\u003e\u003eNeed check w/ vendor.",
      "revId": "512e7e25247011dc5d3d79614a57357787237b9d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ac95911_73d4133e",
        "filename": "driver/als_cm32181e.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-03T11:26:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It it merely read the data registers.\nWe just directly read register and it returned back immediately, but the frequency of data refresh controlled by other register. \nFor example, if we set refresh time as 1.5s, but we read per 0.5s, then we\u0027ll get same value in first 3 reading and get updated value when we do 4th reading.\n\nRefer spec \"table 2\".",
      "parentUuid": "0c2a2473_cc40e0e7",
      "revId": "512e7e25247011dc5d3d79614a57357787237b9d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3d7f981_4aada9d2",
        "filename": "driver/als_cm32181e.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-28T09:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "when rate is 0, ALS should go in suspend mode.\nShould PSM be change depending on the data rate: Mode 3 if rate \u003c 243mHz, Mode 0 otherwise.\n[it is not clear from datasheets what PM modes differences].\n\n\u003e\u003ePSM_SD\u003d1 can shutdown the sensor.\n\u003e\u003eKeep asking vendor for more information about PSM.",
      "revId": "512e7e25247011dc5d3d79614a57357787237b9d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e082a5db_c53c972d",
        "filename": "driver/als_cm32181e.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-03T11:26:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can disable sensor by set ALS_SD in reg 0x00.\nPSM and PSM_EN in reg 0x03 is also using to control refresh time.\n\nRefer spec \"Command Register Format\".",
      "parentUuid": "a3d7f981_4aada9d2",
      "revId": "512e7e25247011dc5d3d79614a57357787237b9d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3625499f_0050be78",
        "filename": "driver/als_cm32181e.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-28T09:47:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "when is drv_data-\u003eoffset updated?\n\nWe use offset for taking care of the glasss in front of the als. We use a linear function: Y \u003d a X + b, where X is the measured value, and Y the real value, a and b coefficients set depending on the glass in front of the ALS. (a, b) depends on the board.\n\n\u003e\u003eThere actually are three coefficient: scale, uscale, offset.\n\u003e\u003eIs it like Y\u003d scale*X + offset?",
      "revId": "512e7e25247011dc5d3d79614a57357787237b9d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
